In Effect-TS, the function used to create an Effect from a generator function is `Generator.from`.

```ts
const effect = Generator.from((a, b) => {
  const sum = a + b;
  return effect.sum(a, b); // This creates an Effect of type Sum(a, b)
});
```

This function takes a generator function as an argument and returns a new Effect. It essentially wraps the generator in a way that handles the return value appropriately, similar to how `Generator.from` works with non-generator functions.

